            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0134" n="968" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg968"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/234a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-21T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>559. Formal announcement was made here on morning of February 20 of relaxation of
                    embargo against Sweden and Holland, giving articles, exportation of which would
                    be permitted. Prospective exporters were instructed that their importer must
                    first notify you of their intention to import and then apply for export license
                    from War Trade Board, and that no British letters of assurance would be issued.
                    The comprehensive plan for the elimination of navicerts, a copy of which you
                    presumably have received from Sheldon, is thus being put into effect. In accordance with that
                    plan you will cable Sheldon of proposed imports and he will notify London Contraband
                    Committee. The War Trade Board, prior to issuing export licenses, will cable
                        Sheldon for
                    recommendation of Contraband Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
